Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:02.930
This is the part of Savannah in Georgia,

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.130
the second largest ports on the east coast.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.350
This map shows ship locations tracked by the company.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:10.760
Marine traffic on August 19,

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:13.340
there was a backup of about 30 container ships.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.370
Similar backlogs have formed at the ports in New York and Hughes.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.810
This is important because it makes life difficult for businesses,

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:24.370
particularly small businesses and it's also important because it helps to keep the cost of 

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:25.730
shipping goods high,

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.920
which contributes to inflation.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:32.050
So how did this backlog happen and what's being done to relieve the congestion?

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:36.220
To understand what's happening today on the east and gulf coast,

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.990
you have to go all the way back to the beginning of the pandemic when there was first a massive 

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.500
decrease in the number of goods moving around the world and then an enormous 

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:50.480
increase of flood of imports that really hasn't stopped for the last two years.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.010
The worst bottlenecks at U.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:52.150
S.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:56.460
Ports have been concentrated at the ports of Los Angeles and Long Beach in southern California,

00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:00.320
where earlier this year there was a backup of more than 100 container ships.

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:01.240
This year,

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.098
cargo growth has slowed at the southern California ports,

00:01:04.188 --> 00:01:04.798
the main U.

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:04.978
S.

00:01:04.978 --> 00:01:06.908
Gateway for goods imported from Asia.

00:01:06.918 --> 00:01:11.548
But volumes headed into the country through the east and gulf coasts have kept rising.

00:01:11.558 --> 00:01:15.738
So retailers and manufacturers had a really really difficult time in 

00:01:15.738 --> 00:01:20.378
2021 getting all of the goods and the widgets that they needed in order to get 

00:01:20.378 --> 00:01:21.998
products to the stores.

00:01:22.008 --> 00:01:26.938
They were so concerned at the start of this year that they would see similar delays to the ones that 

00:01:26.938 --> 00:01:28.178
they saw last year,

00:01:28.478 --> 00:01:33.396
that they both ordered earlier than they norm and they ordered more than they 

00:01:33.406 --> 00:01:34.226
normally would.

00:01:34.296 --> 00:01:38.466
And because retailers and manufacturers were worried about the ports on the west coast,

00:01:38.476 --> 00:01:40.796
they diverted cargo to the ports at new york,

00:01:40.806 --> 00:01:42.166
Houston and savannah.

00:01:42.176 --> 00:01:47.076
Another reason that shippers are diverting cargo from the west Coast this year is because 

00:01:47.076 --> 00:01:51.526
there are labor talks between the union that represents about 22,000 

00:01:51.526 --> 00:01:55.186
dockworkers at all of the ports along the west coast.

00:01:55.196 --> 00:01:56.076
Historically,

00:01:56.076 --> 00:02:00.824
those talks have been contentious and there have been work slowdowns have 

00:02:00.824 --> 00:02:05.664
caused significant delays to cargo during the first five months of the year,

00:02:05.674 --> 00:02:10.644
the volume of loaded containers reaching the port of new york and New Jersey rose more than 12% 

00:02:10.644 --> 00:02:15.424
from the comparable period of 2021 according to the Pacific Merchant Shipping Association,

00:02:15.744 --> 00:02:19.874
the inbound volume import Houston jumped 24% in that period.

00:02:19.884 --> 00:02:24.814
The impact of the congestion at the eastern gulf coast ports is being felt 

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:29.334
both by companies that are trying to import goods into the country as well as by 

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:34.182
export cargo handling terminals at the ports are so full that they load 

00:02:34.182 --> 00:02:35.792
and unload ships more slowly,

00:02:35.802 --> 00:02:38.182
causing backups at sea on land.

00:02:38.192 --> 00:02:42.622
Truckers can't return empty boxes so their yards fill up with containers sitting atop 

00:02:42.622 --> 00:02:43.282
trailers.

00:02:43.292 --> 00:02:48.242
The ports of new york and New Jersey is clogged with about 200,000 empty containers 

00:02:48.252 --> 00:02:51.592
waiting to be picked up by ocean carriers at the Houston ports,

00:02:51.602 --> 00:02:54.772
import boxes are sitting in average of 6 to 7 days,

00:02:54.782 --> 00:02:56.172
twice as long as usual.

00:02:56.182 --> 00:02:58.632
This isn't so much a failure of the ports.

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:04.810
It's more an illustration of what happens when ports become so overwhelmed 

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:05.830
with cargo.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:06.930
At the end of the day,

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:09.710
the ports only have a finite amount of space,

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:13.580
but porch officials say they are taking steps to try to relieve the congestion.

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:18.100
Many of them have found additional land either within their own ports or 

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:22.850
outside of them where they can store extra containers and free up a little bit of 

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:27.190
space so that they can move boxes on and off ships more efficiently.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:32.048
Other officials have talked about charging ocean carriers for empty containers that spent too long at the 

00:03:32.048 --> 00:03:36.608
ports just like the ports on the West Coast and particularly in southern California.

00:03:36.798 --> 00:03:40.398
There's very little in the short term that they can do to alleviate the problem.

00:03:40.408 --> 00:03:41.208
For example,

00:03:41.208 --> 00:03:43.598
dredging channels and installing Ukraine's.

00:03:43.658 --> 00:03:46.008
Those kinds of improvements can take years.

00:03:46.018 --> 00:03:50.788
But shipping officials say a slowdown in cargos might be on the horizon because 

00:03:50.788 --> 00:03:55.748
many importers brought goods in early and because there are significant signs of a 

00:03:55.758 --> 00:03:57.818
slowdown in consumer spending,

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:03.270
some of the shipping industry executives and officials that I spoke to said 

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:06.050
that they expect this year's peak shipping season,

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.970
which we're currently in the middle of,

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:11.140
is expected to be a lot softer than it normally is.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:16.040
Some industry officials are hopeful that in the weeks and months ahead the amount of congestion will 

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:20.340
reduce and the bottlenecks will begin to subside at least a little bit.

